.TH ASK 1 "October 2026" "cli-ask 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ask \- non-intrusive terminal AI assistant with session-scoped context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.I COMMAND
|
.B ask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ask
is a lightweight, zero-dependency command-line utility designed for system administrators, DevOps engineers, and terminal users who want immediate, fluff-free AI answers without disrupting their shell workflow.
.PP
Unlike interactive TUI-based AI assistants, \fBask\fR acts as a native Unix filter: it executes directly from standard command pipelines, streams concise answers directly to standard output, and exits immediately.
.PP
Conversational context is automatically preserved and scoped to the parent shell process ID (PPID). Follow-up questions in the same terminal window retain knowledge of prior turns without cross-contaminating other shell tabs or tmux panes. Long conversations are automatically compacted to maintain responsiveness and avoid token window exhaustion.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clear
Clear the conversation history for the current terminal session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-context
Execute the query as a standalone request without loading or updating the session history.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-key " " \fIAPI_KEY\fR
Save your OpenRouter API key to the user configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Set the default OpenRouter model slug (defaults to \fBnvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-config
Display the current configuration file path, active model, session identifier, and masked API key.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage help and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
If set, overrides the API key saved in the configuration file.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ask/config.json
User configuration containing API credentials and preferred model.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ask/sessions/session\-<PPID>.json
Session-scoped conversation history for the active terminal shell.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Quick command lookup:
ask "how to find listening ports in linux"
.TP
.B Follow-up in same terminal:
ask "filter only tcp ones"
.TP
.B Standard input piping:
git diff | ask "summarize these changes"
.TP
.B Clear active session:
ask --clear

